---
/**
 * The co-design process, redrawn in an essential geometric language:
 * black stroke, transparent fill, nothing else. Requested by Tom 18 Aug 2026
 * from a reference sketch — heavy outlines, overlapping circles, thin arrows,
 * mono uppercase labels, no colour.
 *
 * IT IS A TRANSLATION, NOT AN INVENTION. Every element comes from the studio's
 * own figure, "Milestones of the co-design process with one design iteration",
 * kept in the repo at public/images/co-design-process/01-milestones-one-
 * iteration.webp so this can be checked or reverted. The original already drew
 * Design Meetings and Design Work as two OVERLAPPING circles with the user
 * reality check below — the overlap is the studio's own idea, preserved.
 *
 * People are implied as small dots gathered at each moment of dialogue,
 * densest around the brief and the launch. No faces, no colour.
 *
 * Two purpose-built layouts rather than one scaled figure: a horizontal run for
 * wide viewports, a vertical column below 820px. One SVG scaled to phone width
 * would render its 11px labels at roughly 3px. Both inline, so they inherit
 * --ink and cost no extra request.
 */
